name: Task
description: One unit of work, filed against the Outline section it moves forward.
labels: [task]
body:
  - type: markdown
    attributes:
      value: |
        One issue is one unit of work, so progress stays legible and one assignee owns it. Pick the Outline section this task belongs to; it maps to the `section:N` label and to the matching row in `ROADMAP.md`. The section issues opened by `.github/seed-github.sh` use the same fields, so re-running the script updates them instead of duplicating them.
  - type: input
    id: summary
    attributes:
      label: Outcome
      description: One sentence stating what this task delivers, so a teammate without your context can tell what "done" looks like.
      placeholder: Reconcile the processed totals against the publisher's printed totals.
    validations:
      required: true
  - type: dropdown
    id: section
    attributes:
      label: Outline section
      description: The section of the Outline (https://github.com/CUPIDS-Lab/data-skills/blob/main/OUTLINE.md) this task moves forward. Add the matching `section:N` label.
      options:
        - "1 Scope & gate"
        - "2 Acquire"
        - "3 Extract"
        - "4 Model & tidy"
        - "5 Pipeline & audit"
        - "6 Document & cite"
        - "7 Govern & collaborate"
        - "8 Publish"
        - "9 Deposit, share & discover"
        - "10 Maintain & feedback"
    validations:
      required: true
  - type: textarea
    id: done-when
    attributes:
      label: Done when
      description: Observable checks that must all be true to close this issue. Start from the section's "done when" test in ROADMAP.md.
      value: |
        - [ ]
    validations:
      required: true
  - type: dropdown
    id: priority
    attributes:
      label: Priority
      options:
        - High
        - Medium
        - Low
    validations:
      required: false
  - type: dropdown
    id: size
    attributes:
      label: Size
      description: A rough effort estimate for planning, not a commitment.
      options:
        - S
        - M
        - L
    validations:
      required: false
  - type: dropdown
    id: blocking
    attributes:
      label: Blocking?
      description: Whether this gates another task or a guarded action (ingesting sensitive data, publishing, depositing). If yes, add the `blocking` label and link what it blocks.
      options:
        - "No"
        - "Yes"
    validations:
      required: false
  - type: input
    id: links
    attributes:
      label: Links
      description: The ROADMAP row, sources, prior PRs or decision-log entries that ground the task.
      placeholder: ROADMAP.md section 5; decision-log.md 2026-06-17
    validations:
      required: false
